# **1. Executive Summary**

This report evaluates and designs a residential GPU compute hosting business operating from an owner-controlled property in Hollywood, FL. The analysis spans infrastructure feasibility, compliance architecture, marketplace economics, direct B2B sales strategy, financial modeling, and an 18-month scaling roadmap.

| **Core Thesis** The business model is viable — but the revenue opportunity is not in selling raw GPU hours. It is in selling compliance-packaged private AI infrastructure to regulated South Florida businesses who cannot safely use public AI tools. One private endpoint client at $750/month generates more net cash flow than weeks of marketplace utilization at commodity rates. |
| --- |

