| G4 — Phase 3 expansion | M12 | 4 B2B clients paying. 55%+ marketplace util on 6 GPUs. Cumulative NCF positive. | Add GPU 7+8 ($4,200 CapEx) | Hold at 6 GPUs. Evaluate colocation alternative. |
| G5 — Colo decision | M18 | 5 B2B clients. Revenue target $3,500+/mo NCF. Residential power ceiling approached. | Evaluate Miami/Doral colocation: Tier II/III colo + 20-40 GPU build-out | Remain residential if power headroom exists |

| **Phase 3 Vision — Colocation Migration** If Phase 1 and 2 validate the B2B sales motion, the residential node becomes proof-of-concept for a Miami-area colocation deployment. South Florida colocation (NAP of the Americas, DataBank Miami, QTS Miami) offers Tier II/III infrastructure, 100% uptime SLAs, and unlimited power density — enabling 20-60 GPU deployments that cannot be achieved residentially. The residential operation's compliance posture, client relationships, and brand transfer directly to the colo environment. Phase 3 CapEx: $75,000–150,000. Phase 3 NCF target: $8,000–20,000/month. |
